# ClarityStack: Final Feature Priority List
*Sorted by highest return-on-effort. You have 3 people — split accordingly.*

---

## 🔴 TIER 1: Must-Have (Non-Negotiable — Ship These First)

| # | Feature | Why it's non-negotiable | Effort | Who |
|---|---------|------------------------|--------|-----|
| 1 | **Semantic Search** | Without this, the graph is write-only. People will stop using it in week 2. "Show me all decisions about database architecture" must work even if the original text never used those words. Use a vector embedding (e.g., sentence-transformers) over nodes. | Medium | Backend person |
| 2 | **Decision Provenance Panel** | Every KnowledgeNode must link back to the exact message(s) that created it. This is your Git Blame moment. It is the single feature that makes ClarityStack fundamentally different from Notion AI. Without it, no professional trusts the graph as source of truth. | Medium | Backend + Frontend |
| 3 | **Visual Graph View** | Right now the graph exists as a database but users see cards/lists. You must render an actual interactive node graph (use `react-force-graph` or `vis-network`). This is the one screenshot that will make investors, professors, and recruiters stop scrolling. | Medium | Frontend person |
| 4 | **User Auth + Workspaces** | Right now any call to the API exposes all projects. Need JWT-based auth and project-level access roles (Admin, Contributor, Viewer). Without this, no team-use, no B2B pitch, no enterprise conversation. | Medium | Backend |
| 5 | **Import via Paste** | A dedicated "Import Chat" page where you paste a raw ChatGPT, Claude, or Slack conversation and it automatically splits it into a thread, runs classification, and feeds it through your synthesis pipeline. This reduces the barrier to getting data in to near-zero. | Low-Medium | Backend + Frontend |

