## 🟡 TIER 2: High Value (Ship These Next — Major Differentiators)

| # | Feature | Why it matters | Effort | Who |
|---|---------|---------------|--------|-----|
| 6 | **"Today" Dashboard / Daily Briefing** | On login, show: contested nodes awaiting resolution, stale decisions (not updated in 60+ days), and recent team activity. This creates a daily open-the-app habit, which is the difference between a tool and a workflow. | Medium | Frontend + Backend |
| 7 | **Conflict Resolution Workflow** | When AI detects a CONFLICT edge between two nodes, it raises a "Resolution Required" flag. A designated owner (PM, lead) sees it on their dashboard and clicks "Approve A / Approve B / Rewrite." This is human-in-the-loop governance — critical for teams and enterprise. | Medium-High | Full stack |
| 8 | **Chrome Extension (Clip to Graph)** | Highlight any text on any webpage (research paper, documentation, Slack in browser) and right-click → "Add to ClarityStack." It creates a KnowledgeNode instantly. Researchers will never leave after this. | Medium | New frontend skill |
| 9 | **Export: Audit Pack** | One-click export of all decisions in a project as a structured PDF or JSON-LD, with timestamps, node IDs, source message references, and model used. Essential for compliance, thesis appendices, and board-level reviews. | Low | Backend |
| 10 | **Temporal Confidence Decay** | A nightly background job that slowly reduces `confidence` on any `KnowledgeNode` not reinforced by new input in 90 days and flags it `STALE`. Shows the graph is a living system, not a dump. Huge for your resume (temporal reasoning in applied systems). | Low | Backend |

